--- OLD
  @PtrLoaded:             ; here, text_ptr points to the desired string
--- NEW
;  Chest Information draws its description by entering here, with text_ptr
;  already pointing at it.  It has to be this routine rather than
;  DrawComplexString: the dialogue box straddles the two nametables, and only
;  this one advances dest_x with AND #$3F and resets the PPU address when the
;  boundary is crossed.  A global label rather than a cheap one so it can be
;  imported -- which is why the jump above names it too.
.export DrawDialogueString_PtrLoaded
.import rando_dlgtext
DrawDialogueString_PtrLoaded:
                          ; here, text_ptr points to the desired string
    ;  ...unless a reward NPC has just given what placement put there: then
    ;  its line, naming that, built far (rando_dlgtext).  Otherwise nothing.
    JSL rando_dlgtext + RANDOFAR
